        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "-2"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "2"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "10"
          }
        ],
        "correctOptionId": "a"
      },
      "explanation": "For a 2 by 2 matrix, the determinant is ad minus bc: 1 times 4 minus 2 times 3 equals -2."
    },
    {
      "id": "fm-invertible",
      "topicId": "matrices",
      "topicLabel": "Matrices",
      "prompt": "For a square matrix, what does a non-zero determinant tell you?",
